feasible.corrections:
- Threat coverage is overstated. The check proves "digest matches calldata", not "the device showed X". It gives zero defence against a compromised image, a renderer bug, or a confirm/page-skip fault. For Safe, CoW and ERC-7730 shapes it degenerates to BLIND‖calldataDigest, so "closes the gap for >80% of drain value" is unsupported.
- The repo_evidence line "ladder already yields a discrete intent class" misleads. The ladder class is a render route, not an on-chain-recomputable class: an ERC-20 transfer can render via ERC-7730, known ERC-20 or shape-only ERC-20.
- "No address change constraints beyond re-pinning codehashes" is wrong. The wallet is non-upgradeable, so this needs a new implementation, a new factory, new PQ_SMART_WALLET_FACTORY / PROXY_INIT_CODE_HASH / EXECUTE_SELECTOR / MAX_EXECUTE_CALLDATA_LEN, a new initCode, and new wallet addresses on every chain. The Base Mainnet deployment would be abandoned.
- Cost is XL, not L. On top of the redeploy it must:
  - rerun Halmos (42 rules), Kontrol and DeployedBytecodeReproCheck;
  - redo the Lean wallet model (Wallet/Execute.lean, TxFlow.lean, OffchainBinding.lean and the bytecode↔AST transcription);
  - add a per-record digest to executeBatchWithOffchainCount and the CMD 30 handler (the proposal omits the batch path);
  - update companion calldata building and the usb-protocol docs;
  - add a three-way frozen grammar across Solidity, Rust and Lean.
- New liveness risk: with an immutable implementation, any grammar mismatch makes that shape revert at execution after slotUses was already bumped in validation, burning C10 budget and gas until a firmware fix.
- Kind "mixed" is right as firmware + contract; there is no hardware element.
- Precedent: correctly "none shipped", and no Trezor code is cited, so there was nothing to grep. EIP-719 concerns a dapp-supplied signing-UI description, not on-chain execution enforcement, so it is a loose analogy only. The ethresear.ch 21836 citation was not fetched or verified.
- Salvage (S, firmware/process): promote the existing host differential "rendered operands == operands decoded from signed bytes" into a Kani harness and extend it to the batch and ui-px routes. This gets the one real property without touching the contract.
